From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: sidebar: the rail expands on hover after a pause the user sets

The collapsed rail expanded the moment the pointer arrived: Chromium's
350 ms, and its velocity heuristic that opens sooner still when the pointer
heads into the strip, so a tab in the rail could not be clicked without the
sidebar opening on top of the click (operator, 2026-09-09).

- A profile preference, stedding.sidebar.hover_delay_ms, 2000 by default:
  the pause before the rail expands. VerticalTabStripRegionView starts its
  expand timer with it under the Arc window and leaves the velocity
  heuristic aside; a click in the rail restarts the wait, so a tab can be
  chosen and the pointer moved on. Zero keeps Chromium's own timing.
- One row in chrome://settings/stedding: "Open the collapsed sidebar on
  hover" -- after 0.35 seconds (Chromium's timing), 1, 2 or 5 seconds
  (settings T11).

Why: docs/features/sidebar.md Y11.
Removable when: upstream's expand-on-hover delay becomes a preference of its
own with a click that restarts it.
